# CORRECTION: tap ownership is NOT a defect.
#
# Earlier hypothesis: nwd creates taps without `user chv`, so CH as uid 999
# cannot TUNSETIFF. That hypothesis is wrong. `ip tuntap add ... mode tap`
# executed by a process holding CAP_NET_ADMIN (nwd's context) creates the
# device with no TUNSETOWNER, i.e. kernel owner == -1, which is attachable by
# any uid. The observed EPERM was at open(/dev/net/tun) from the agent unit's
# device cgroup, not at TUNSETIFF.

